      "title": "Batshit Qwen 360 Skybox Notes",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "This is the visible Comfy Desktop copy of the Batshit skybox workflow. The agent/MCP template ships with Batshit at `batshit-app/src/lib/server/system-skills/goon-scene-creator/assets/comfyui/qwen360-skybox-api-workflow.json`.\n\nUse this for 2:1 equirectangular Room Builder skyboxes. The workflow generates a 2048x1024 base and upscales to 4096x2048 with Real-ESRGAN x2. For the recommended final Hero 8K export, run another x2 upscale pass or use the agent workflow defaults. Standard 4K is the smaller/lower-memory Mac or PC and performance-fallback path.\n\nThe default positive and negative prompt nodes are Ground Level defaults. Ground Level rule: target the exact equirectangular equator at 50% image height. Everything below it must be continuous projectable ground/floor only; keep nearby furniture, walls, screens, buildings, trees, rocks, columns, and other upright objects out of the lower hemisphere. Add `true 360 degree equirectangular panorama`, `seamless horizontal wrap`, and `8K texture detail`. Before handoff, overlay an exact 50% guide on the flat panorama and inspect it in Batshit Ground Level mode.\n\nFor Elevated / Overlook, replace BOTH prompt nodes. Use an elevated/open distant-world positive prompt and remove the Ground Level equator/lower-ground negatives; do not leave contradictory Ground Level restrictions active."
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
